{"title":"Logic","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Logic</b> is the systematic use of symbolic and mathematical techniques to determine the forms of valid deductive or inductive argument. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statements\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statements</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Conditional\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Conditional</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Inverse\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inverse</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Converse\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Converse</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Contrapositive\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Contrapositive</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Logical_Notations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Logical Notations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Implication\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Implication</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Negations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Negations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Conjunction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Conjunction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Disjunction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Disjunction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Implication,_Conditional\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Implication, Conditional</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Converse_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Converse</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Inverse_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Inverse</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Contrapositive_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Contrapositive</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Truth_Tables\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Truth Tables</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Quantifiers\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quantifiers</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statements\">Statements</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statements\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Statement&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Statement (page does not exist)\">statement</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>A statement is either true or false, but it will never be both or neither. An example of a statement is \"A duck is a bird\" which is true. Another example is \"A pencil does not exist\" which is false.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conditional\">Conditional</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Conditional\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Conditional\" title=\"Conditional\">conditional</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. For example, \"If it is a duck then it is a bird.\"\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inverse\">Inverse</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Inverse\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inverse\" title=\"Inverse\">inverse</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The inverse of the conditional statement is: If not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> then not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Converse\">Converse</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Converse\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Converse\" title=\"Converse\">converse</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The converse of the conditional statement is: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contrapositive\">Contrapositive</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Contrapositive\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Contrapositive\" title=\"Contrapositive\">contrapositive</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The contrapositive of the conditional statement is: If not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> then not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The conditional is equivalent to the contrapositive. The inverse is equivalent to the converse. When both the conditional and the converse are true at the same time, this is equivalent to an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=If_and_only_if&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"If and only if (page does not exist)\">if and only if</a> statement.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Logical_Notations\">Logical Notations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Logical Notations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logical_notation&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Logical notation (page does not exist)\">Logical notation</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p><b>Logical notation</b> is a special syntax that is shorthand for logical statements. \n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Implication\">Implication</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Implication\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The implication between two statements is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b8d4c570eda8c0523dcb5236379ee47e2358d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\implies q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Negations\">Negations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Negations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The negation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7277906db97e80af8fe4f7357ee5e430871164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neg p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"21\" height=\"11\" />, is the statement that is true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is false and is false when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is true. This means simply \"it is not the case that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\"\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conjunction\">Conjunction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Conjunction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The conjunction of two statements basically means \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\" and is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/c/afc05e5cc6b26e8365374c2f45f8a0a6bc506195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\land q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Disjunction\">Disjunction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Disjunction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The disjunction of two statements basically means \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\" and is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9c83a370f85c8f7655f882f50bb2024e985fc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\vee q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Implication.2C_Conditional\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Implication,_Conditional\">Implication, Conditional</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Implication, Conditional\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The statement \"If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\" is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/9/179a2ebda4e4b92520f3459c93393a481d3c39f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\implies q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caad664838895bc66aadf956afb45118ade74839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+3=5\\implies x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"14\" /> means \"If  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/69038b45c5cb5cdb540f7be31ab89e5832f2f27d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+3=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\"\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Converse_2\">Converse</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Converse\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The converse of the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b8d4c570eda8c0523dcb5236379ee47e2358d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\implies q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/f/a1fffe8ddebf353428ed42d0a029835ac1b7a526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q \\implies p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Inverse_2\">Inverse</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Inverse\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The inverse of the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b8d4c570eda8c0523dcb5236379ee47e2358d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\implies q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636d972c37b954220c6e6a89e251685693450429.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neg p \\implies \\neg q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Contrapositive_2\">Contrapositive</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Contrapositive\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The contrapositive of the statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b8d4c570eda8c0523dcb5236379ee47e2358d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\implies q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412f2e145fdb015a3f3eee503b3e67aa3f6f5eb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\neg q \\implies \\neg p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. These statements are logically equivalent.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Truth_Tables\">Truth Tables</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Truth Tables\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A truth table is the list of all possible values of a compound statement.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quantifiers\">Quantifiers</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Quantifiers\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two types of quantifiers: A universal Quantifier: \"for all\" and an existential Quantifier: \"there exists\". A universal quantifier is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536ba5a392431e74fec5a8db2257504c85fcc206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> and an existential quantifier is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/c/4ecf8666cca5f1d089b9c656be83f9e09d0abd5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\exists$\" width=\"9\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dual\" title=\"Dual\">Dual</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Logic&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018093612\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 288/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 686/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 238/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5946/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   24.694      1 -total\n 55.17%   13.624      6 Template:Main\n 26.34%    6.505      6 Template:Hatnote\n 23.74%    5.863      1 Template:Stub\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5452:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018093612 and revision id 259523. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}